    {
      "path": "content/Adventures/DM Notes/FLS/Tier 2/Wyvern and the Wyrmhole.md",
      "ok": true,
      "totalLines": 369,
      "returnedRange": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "endLine": 132
      },
      "hasMoreBelow": true,
      "nextStartLine": 133,
      "content": "92|> **Retrieve the dead drop. Do not alert the authorities.**\n93|\n94|The advertisement leads the characters to **the third rusted shrine-box along the Sootsteps in [[Upper South Booftown]]**, a soot-stained stairway shrine wedged between stacked tenements, rope bridges, and rooftop shortcuts. Locals leave burnt incense, copper bits, cheap liquor, and handwritten grudges there for whatever street spirit still listens.\n95|\n96|To open the dead drop, a character must knock twice, whisper **“Gravity squeezes harder,”** and lift the hidden compartment beneath the offering tray. Inside is a black envelope, a sealed case containing a mundane sword, and a phial of Robust Essence. No Society representative appears. A second document inside the envelope describes the creature the Society wants them to create and harvest.\n97|\n98|### Dead Drop Encounter\n99|\n100|Roll or choose one encounter when the characters arrive at the shrine-box.\n101|\n102|| d4 | Encounter |\n103||---:|---|\n104|| 1 | **MOB Lookouts.** Two [[Mandem on Booftown]] lookouts are using the shrine as a watching post. They do not know about the dead drop, but they notice if the party acts suspiciously. A small bribe, good lie, or local name gets them to look away. |\n105|| 2 | **CCC Collection Crew.** A pair of [[Cough City Crew]] toughs arrive to collect “shrine tax” from nearby vendors. If they see the party retrieve the case, they assume it is valuable contraband and demand a cut. |\n106|| 3 | **Ashfall Beggar.** An elderly local beggar warns the characters that the shrine-box “only opens for people already in trouble.” They have seen other dead drops here before and can share a rumor about the [[Ashen Shadow Society]] for coin, food, or kindness. |\n107|| 4 | **Watched from Above.** A hidden Society observer watches from a rooftop across the alley. They do not intervene unless the party botches the retrieval or attracts too much attention. If followed, they flee across the Sootsteps and vanish into the ash. |\n108|\n109|Read or paraphrase the following:\n110|\n111|> The Sootsteps climb above the street in crooked layers of stairs, ladders, rope bridges, and patched balconies. Ash from [[Mount Zooka]] dusts every rail and rooftop.\n112|>\n113|> The third shrine-box is rusted almost shut, its little roof stained black by old incense smoke. Someone has left a cracked cup of liquor, three copper coins, and a folded note that simply reads, *“Make him pay.”*\n114|>\n115|> No one waits beside it. No one openly watches. But the alley is too quiet, and every dark window feels occupied.\n116|>\n117|> After two knocks and the whispered phrase, the offering tray clicks loose. Hidden beneath it is a black envelope sealed with a stylized ash-gray eye surrounded by hooked lines, beside a narrow sealed case and a small phial of thick essence.\n118|>\n119|> When the envelope seal breaks, it releases the smell of hot metal, old smoke, and something faintly organic.\n120|>\n121|> Inside is a contract bearing a single designation:\n122|>\n123|> **OPERATION: GRAVITY SQUEEZE**\n124|>\n125|> A folded document lies beneath the contract. Its paper is thick, its ink is dark, and its final page has been sealed with black wax.\n126|>\n127|> The contract lists the Society’s requirements:\n128|>\n129|> 1. Travel into the wilderness and hunt down a wyvern.\n130|> 2. Preserve the wyvern’s corpse without harvesting it or damaging its heart.\n131|> 3. Use the supplied Mind Blade in the corpse’s heart and perform the enclosed rite.\n132|> 4. Defeat the creature created by the rite.",
      "wikilinks": [
        {
          "link": "Upper South Booftown",
